.TH GOLDENRECORD 1 2000-1月 "as.bitmap" "as.bitmap"
.SH NAME
as.bitmap \- render the decoded pixels as a gray scale or a pseudo color bitmap image.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIas.bitmap(\fBpixels\fR as <generic> PixelDecode, 
\fBluminous\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBwhite\fR as double = 1, 
\fBgamma\fR as double = 1, 
\fBinvert\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBpercentile\fR as double = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBpalette\fR as string = "gray", 
\fBsmooth\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBheight\fR as integer = 0);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
render the decoded pixels as a gray scale or a pseudo color bitmap image.
 
 the intensity data is normalized by the percentile based auto levels, and the
 polarity is inverted by default because the image data of the golden record is
 stored as a photographic negative.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBpixels\fB \fR\- -. 
.PP
.PP
\fBluminous\fB \fR\- render as a pseudo color image. 
.PP
.PP
\fBwhite\fB \fR\- the white point gain, 0 or 1 means no adjustment. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgamma\fB \fR\- the gamma correction, 1 means no correction. 
.PP
.PP
\fBinvert\fB \fR\- the black/white polarity. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpercentile\fB \fR\- the black point and the white point percentiles, like \fBc(0.005, 0.995)\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpalette\fB \fR\- the palette name of the pseudo color rendering. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsmooth\fB \fR\- the radius of the across scan line smoothing, 0 for disable. 
.PP
.PP
\fBheight\fB \fR\- the output image height in pixels, 0 for keep the original size. 
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
goldenRecord
.SH FILES
.PP
